SUMMARY:Josh Johnson's Comedy Band Camp LIVE at Orpheum Theatre Minneapolis
	 (Early Show)
DTSTAMP:20260815T032443Z
DTSTART:20260815T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:This post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at
	 no extra cost to you. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Perfor
	mer\nJosh Johnson is a rising star in stand-up comedy\, best known as a wr
	iter and correspondent on The Daily Show\, where his sharp political wit a
	nd incisive cultural commentary earned him an Emmy nomination. \nHis comed
	y blends intelligent observation with absurdist humor\, tackling race\, po
	litics\, and everyday life with a style that is both thought-provoking and
	 laugh-out-loud funny. Johnson has quickly become one of the most talked-a
	bout voices in modern comedy. \nThe Comedy Band Camp concept is a unique\,
	 immersive comedy experience — part stand-up show\, part live performance 
	spectacle — that has been selling out theaters across the country on its 2
	026 tour. \nEvent Details\nDate: Saturday\, August 15\, 2026 \nTime: 5:00 
	PM (Early Show) \nVenue: Orpheum Theatre Minneapolis\, 910 Hennepin Avenue
	\, Minneapolis\, MN 55403 \nTicket Prices: $59.75 – $175 \nAge Restriction
	s: All ages welcome\; some content may be intended for mature audiences. \
	nAbout the Venue\nThe Orpheum Theatre is one of Minneapolis’s most iconic 
	and beloved performance venues\, located in the heart of the city’s vibran
	t Theater District on Hennepin Avenue. \nBuilt in 1921\, the Orpheum seats
	 approximately 2\,600 guests and features stunning historic architecture\,
	 ornate interior design\, and exceptional acoustics that make every show f
	eel special. The venue is operated by Hennepin Theatre Trust and is renown
	ed for hosting Broadway productions\, major concerts\, and top-tier comedy
	 acts. \nThe Orpheum offers a mix of reserved seating options across the o
	rchestra\, mezzanine\, and balcony levels. Amenities include multiple bars
	\, concession stands\, and accessible seating. Parking is available in nea
	rby downtown Minneapolis ramps\, and the venue is easily accessible via Me
	tro Transit light rail (Nicollet Mall Station is a short walk away). \nWha
	t to Expect\nJosh Johnson’s Comedy Band Camp is not your average stand-up 
	show. Expect a high-energy\, theatrical comedy experience that combines Jo
	hnson’s razor-sharp stand-up with live musical elements and a uniquely imm
	ersive format that has wowed audiences nationwide. \nThis is the early sho
	w on Saturday\, August 15 — doors typically open 30–45 minutes before show
	time. The performance runs approximately 90 minutes. Arrive early to grab 
	a drink at the bar and soak in the gorgeous Orpheum atmosphere before the 
	show begins. \nWhether you’re a longtime fan of Josh Johnson from The Dail
	y Show or discovering him for the first time\, this is a must-see comedy e
	vent in Minneapolis this summer. \nTicket Information\nTickets range from 
	$59.75 to $175 depending on seat location. Official tickets are available 
	through Ticketmaster. Resale tickets are available through VividSeats. \nO
	fficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may
	 earn a commission at no extra cost to you.\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/
	event/josh-johnsons-comedy-band-camp-live-at-orpheum-theatre-minneapolis-e
	arly-show/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/josh-johnsons-comedy-band-camp-live-at
	-orpheum-theatre-minneapolis-early-show/
LOCATION:Orpheum Theatre Minneapolis\, 910 Hennepin Avenue\, Minneapolis\, 
	MN\, 55403
